{"events":[{"tStartMs":0,"dDurationMs":12700,"segs":[{"utf8":"I needed a shelf that sits over a radiator without cooking whatever is on it, and nobody sells one that is the right depth, so this is the afternoon it took to build."}]},{"tStartMs":12700,"dDurationMs":11500,"segs":[{"utf8":"The timber is ordinary pine, planed on three sides, and the whole lot came to less than a takeaway, which is the correct budget for a first attempt at anything."}]},{"tStartMs":24200,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"I cut the two uprights first, because a mistake there costs one board rather than the whole frame, and because everything else gets measured off them anyway."}]},{"tStartMs":34600,"dDurationMs":10000,"segs":[{"utf8":"Getting the frame clamped square is the entire job, honestly, everything after that is just driving screws and pretending you meant the gap to be there."}]},{"tStartMs":44600,"dDurationMs":11500,"segs":[{"utf8":"A pilot hole two millimetres under the screw diameter stops pine splitting at the end grain, and near a radiator the wood moves enough that a split will open up."}]},{"tStartMs":56100,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"I left the top overhanging the radiator by twenty millimetres at the back so the hot air has somewhere to go instead of sitting under the shelf."}]},{"tStartMs":66500,"dDurationMs":10800,"segs":[{"utf8":"The brackets are the cheap steel ones from the hardware shop, turned upside down, which puts the long arm against the wall where the load actually wants it."}]},{"tStartMs":77300,"dDurationMs":10000,"segs":[{"utf8":"Before the finish goes on, a quick word from Squarespace, who are supporting this build and who host the site where all of these plans live."}]},{"tStartMs":87300,"dDurationMs":10800,"segs":[{"utf8":"I put this shelf up as a page with the cut list and the measurements in an afternoon, which is about as long as the shelf itself took."}]},{"tStartMs":98100,"dDurationMs":10000,"segs":[{"utf8":"Head to squarespace dot com slash radiator for ten percent off your first site or domain, and the trial does not want a card up front."}]},{"tStartMs":108100,"dDurationMs":3500,"segs":[{"utf8":"That is the whole ad, back to the oil."}]},{"tStartMs":111600,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"Two coats of hardwax oil, sanded lightly between them with two twenty grit, and a third coat on the top surface because that is where mugs land."}]},{"tStartMs":122000,"dDurationMs":11200,"segs":[{"utf8":"It has been on the wall for a month over a radiator that runs hot every evening and the joint at the left upright has not moved at all."}]},{"tStartMs":133200,"dDurationMs":10400,"segs":[{"utf8":"If your radiator runs hotter than mine, or it is a thin panel one that sits close to the wall, leave a bigger gap than twenty millimetres."}]},{"tStartMs":143600,"dDurationMs":9200,"segs":[{"utf8":"The one thing I would change is the depth, another three centimetres would let a book lie flat instead of overhanging the front edge."}]},{"tStartMs":152800,"dDurationMs":5400,"segs":[{"utf8":"The plans and the cut list are in the description, and thanks for watching."}]}]}